---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import Button from '../components/Button.astro'

const offers = [
  {
    name: 'System found',
    price: '$10,000',
    period: 'one week',
    description: 'Dylan finds the design system your code already has and makes it real, so your coding agents stop inventing new values.',
    items: [
      'A full Buoy baseline of one frontend codebase',
      'Your color, spacing and type sprawl consolidated into tokens and a theme',
      'A DESIGN.md your team and your agents can read',
      'Agent rules and MCP setup for Cursor, Claude Code or the agent you already use',
      'A before-and-after report',
    ],
  },
  {
    name: 'System in place',
    price: '$20,000',
    period: 'two weeks',
    featured: true,
    description: 'Everything in System found, then the code is moved onto it, so the product looks like one product.',
    items: [
      'Everything in System found',
      'Your worst components migrated, in pull requests your team reviews and merges',
      'The Buoy GitHub App set up so new drift is caught on every pull request',
      'A first adoption baseline and a 30-day recheck',
    ],
  },
  {
    name: 'Keep it holding',
    price: '$1,500',
    period: 'per month, per product',
    description: 'After a sprint, Dylan keeps watching so the system holds as your agents write more of the code.',
    items: [
      'Team plan included',
      'A monthly adoption report, with agent-written pull requests split out',
      'A monthly review call with Dylan',
    ],
  },
]
---

<Layout
  title="Work with Dylan | Buoy"
  description="System found: $10,000 for one week. System in place: $20,000 for two weeks. Keep it holding: $1,500 a month per product."
>
  <Nav />

  <main>
    <section class="relative pt-32 pb-20 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-navy-dark via-navy to-navy-dark"></div>
      <div class="absolute top-1/2 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-96 h-96 bg-sunrise/10 rounded-full blur-3xl"></div>
      <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-full bg-sunrise/10 border border-sunrise/30 mb-6">
          <span class="text-sunrise font-medium text-sm">Work with Dylan · from $10,000</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-bold text-light mb-6">
          Keep AI-generated UI<br />true to your product.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-10">
          Dylan uses Buoy to find the design system your code already has, turn it into tokens and rules your coding agents follow, and move your product onto it. One or two weeks, fixed price.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
          <Button href="https://cal.com/tarre/rescue" size="lg" external>
            Talk to Dylan →
          </Button>
          <Button href="#what-you-get" variant="secondary" size="lg">
            See what you get
          </Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-navy border-y border-navy-light/20">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center">
          <div>
            <p class="text-buoy font-medium mb-3">The missing layer</p>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-light mb-4">A design system gives AI the parts. Buoy gives it context and judgment.</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate text-lg">
            Coding agents can assemble a valid interface and still produce something generic, off-brand, or wrong for the moment. Buoy connects product intent to implementation: what to use, why it belongs, and what should never ship.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="what-you-get" class="py-20 bg-navy-dark scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
          {offers.map((offer) => (
            <article class={`flex flex-col bg-navy/50 border rounded-2xl p-8 ${offer.featured ? 'border-buoy' : 'border-navy-light/20'}`}>
              <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-light mb-1">{offer.name}</h2>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 gap-y-1 mb-4">
                <span class="text-3xl font-bold text-light">{offer.price}</span>
                <span class="text-slate text-sm">{offer.period}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate mb-6">{offer.description}</p>
              <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate">
                {offer.items.map((item) => (
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-success">✓</span>
                    <span>{item}</span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-12 bg-navy border border-buoy/30 rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-light mb-4">What Buoy will—and will not—automate</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate">
            <li>Tokens, components, accessibility, and supported code rules can be enforced deterministically.</li>
            <li>Hierarchy, mood, and brand expression remain documented guidance until the evidence is strong.</li>
            <li>Ambiguous findings stay review-required.</li>
            <li>Fixes land on branches with visible diffs and existing checks.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate border-t border-navy-light/20 mt-6 pt-6">Sprints are fixed price: half to begin, half at handoff. Just want the GitHub App? See <a href="/pricing" class="text-buoy hover:underline">pricing</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-20 bg-navy-dark">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <article class="border border-success/30 rounded-xl p-7">
            <p class="text-success font-medium mb-3">A strong fit</p>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-light mb-4">Your product already has an identity worth protecting.</h2>
            <p class="text-slate">
              You have a working frontend, an existing component library or recognizable product language, and a team using AI to ship UI faster.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="border border-navy-light/20 rounded-xl p-7">
            <p class="text-slate font-medium mb-3">Not the right plan</p>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-light mb-4">You need someone to invent the entire brand from scratch.</h2>
            <p class="text-slate">
              A sprint puts existing product judgment to work. It is not a replacement for foundational brand strategy or zero-to-one product design.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-20 bg-navy">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-light mb-4">Start with evidence from your codebase.</h2>
        <p class="text-slate text-lg mb-8">
          Run Buoy locally or bring one representative UI pull request. We will use the actual product and implementation to decide which sprint fits, if any.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-navy-dark border border-navy-light/30 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-left">
          <code class="text-buoy">npx ahoybuoy show health</code>
        </div>
        <Button href="https://cal.com/tarre/rescue" size="lg" external>
          Talk to Dylan →
        </Button>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate mt-4">No commitment. No invented ROI math. We will tell you if the product is not ready for this.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
